Changelog: 15-11-2026 07:05:26

Fixed. tools/ci-local.sh runs one at a time on a computer: a second run says that another one is going and waits
until it ends (owner, 15-11-2026: two runs at once shared the venvs and the logs, a Qt test crashed and a run never
ended).

Changelog: 15-11-2026 06:25:12

Added. tools/check-release.sh cleans up after a test, as the Bazzite Console Suite's does (owner, 15-11-2026): on
a board without the suite, what a test installs (local, release or draft, the Device test too) is marked as a
test's and removed again when the portal closes; a board that had the suite keeps it, and --keep keeps what a test
installed. check-release.sh status lists what of the suite is installed and whether a test put it there, and
check-release.sh remove [--purge] removes it all, every app, the portal and Board Test, each with its own
uninstaller. release takes the draft while the release is not published yet. tools/installer-tests/release-check.sh
tests it all.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 05:52:56

Fixed. tools/pre-push.sh's message for a missing portal bump names Nexus Release Tool's Commit your changes, which
offers the bump, instead of its Bump portal, which is gone; DESIGN.md names the tool's main actions as they are now.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 03:58:53

Breaking. Eight apps are new apps (owner, 15-11-2026): BC-250 Webcam, BC-250 Controller, BC-250 Turing Screen,
BC-250 System Overlay, BC-250 SFTP Tools, BC-250 SSD Check, BC-250 Wi-Fi Adapter and BC-250 Board Test (Board Test
for short), each with its own id, folders, launcher, settings and release tags; the keys of four of them are webcam,
controller, turing and wifi. The wiki (its chapters apps/webcam, apps/controller, apps/turing, apps/wifi and
development/board-test*), the README, DESIGN.md (from tools/make_design.py), the workflows and the tools name them
so. A copy installed before is not taken over: uninstall it first.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 03:22:26

Added. tools/installer-tests/not-installed.sh runs every app's and the portal's install.sh --uninstall, and with
--purge, on a computer where nothing is installed: each says so in one line, exits 0, writes nothing and asks for no
sudo password (owner, 15-11-2026).

Changelog: 15-11-2026 02:59:45

Added. The wiki's Bluetooth Pairing chapter has a section on a USB 3 device beside the Bluetooth receiver: it can
heavily interfere with it, and a USB extension cable that keeps the two as far apart as possible helps.

