Changelog: 15-11-2026 02:03:59

Breaking. The release tags start with bc250- (owner, 15-11-2026): bc250-<app>-v<x.y.z> and bc250-portal-v<x.y.z>, the
prefix in the new TAG_PREFIX file, as the Bazzite Console Suite's start with ps5-. The releases made in Nexus keep
their plain tags. portal/apps.toml pins the bc250- tags; the portal's manifest, tools/check_manifest.py,
tools/pin_app.py, tools/suite_release.py, tools/publish_release.sh (a bc250-portal-v release is GitHub's Latest),
tools/check-release.sh, tools/tag-release.sh, release.yml (the portal's checks, PS Remote Play's wheel, the Windows
executable's app) and the installer tests use them; tools/build_release.py, Nexus Release Tool and the tours read the
prefix from TAG_PREFIX. The wiki's tags and file names follow.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 01:35:46

Added. DESIGN.md and its color samples in design/colors/ are back, as the Bazzite Console Suite has them (owner,
15-11-2026): every color of the suite, where it is defined and what it is for, written by tools/make_design.py (taken
over from Nexus, with the suite's colors alone: the BC250 rules, the color families, the apps' themes and state
colors, the wiki, the development apps' Nexus design, the apps' own colors and the portal screenshot's palette).
tools/make_design.py --check, run by tools/tests, says when DESIGN.md or a sample is out of date, and when the wiki's
stylesheet and the listing disagree. The block samples are the same files Nexus had; the text samples show a sentence
about the suite instead of one about Nexus.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 01:08:09

Fixed. The code paths for a suite made for Windows devices are gone from the tools (owner, 15-11-2026): new_app.py's
Windows template, build_release.py's refusal of a Windows suite's tag, ci_matrix.py's installers matrix and
core-first order, sync_icons.py's PNG and wide icons ([icons] format and wide), and the Windows system in suites.py
(SYSTEM is bazzite). Their tests went with them. Core, Nexus Release Tool, Nexus Dashboard, Nexus Installer Tests and
Nexus Demo Recorder lost theirs too (their CHANGELOGs). The development apps still run on Windows where they did, and
SFTP Tools keeps its Windows executable.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 23:58:33

Breaking. The BC250 Bazzite Suite is a repository of its own, github.com/RobertoTorino/bc250-bazzite (owner,
14-11-2026: one repository per suite, standalone with its own tooling, as the Bazzite Console Suite). Its files were
the folder bc250-bazzite/ of github.com/RobertoTorino/nexus and are now this repository's root: portal/, apps/,
docs/ with mkdocs.yml, icons/, install.sh and tools/. What it took from Nexus is its own now: core/ (bc250_core,
bundled in every app), the tools (the release and CI tools, the design panel and the disclaimer hook, the tours'
shared code and music, sync_icons.py, new_app.py), the development apps in dev/ (Nexus Dashboard, Nexus Release Tool,
Nexus Demo Recorder, Nexus Installer Tests, Nexus Sound Lab, Nexus Deps), test.sh and the root's files. The history
of these files stays in Nexus.

The releases are made here, with the same tags (<app>-v<x.y.z>, portal-v<x.y.z>), and the apps and the portal look
for them here; GitHub's Latest release is the newest portal. A portal or app installed from a release made in Nexus
keeps looking there and sees no newer release: installing the portal from this repository's latest release once
brings it here. The wiki is at robertotorino.github.io/bc250-bazzite/, built by this repository's docs.yml.

ci.yml runs every check on every push: the suite's and those that ran in Nexus's ci-nexus.yml (core, tools, dev/,
line endings, exec bits, the four files of every folder, workflows only at the root). release.yml is started by Nexus
Release Tool's Start new release on the release commit, or by hand (gh workflow run release.yml -f commit=...), and
waits for ci.yml alone. Gone with Nexus: the root's copy of portal/apps.toml (pin_app.py, suite_release.py,
check_manifest.py and new_app.py no longer write or compare it), the Nexus release and its version, the Nexus index,
the wait for ci-nexus.yml (tag-release.sh, release.yml, ci_local.py), make_icons.py and ICONS.md, and the tests of
Nexus's own rules for several suites. The tools find the suite at the root (tools/suites.py names it "."), and their
paths, the installer tests and the wiki's hooks are written for that layout.
